### Amazon Sales Performance Analysis
**Advanced Excel | Data Analyst Project**

In this project, I worked on an Amazon Sales Performance Analysis using Microsoft Excel. The main goal was to understand sales performance,
customer purchasing behaviour, product demand, and order status over a three-month period from February to April 2025.

I started by understanding the dataset and checking its quality. The dataset contained 250 order records and 12 columns, including Order ID, Date, 
Product, Category, Price, Quantity, Total Sales, Customer Name, Customer Location, Payment Method, and Order Status.

After understanding the data, I performed data cleaning and validation. I checked for missing values, duplicate records, incorrect formats, and inconsistent entries. 
I also verified the sales calculations to make sure the Total Sales values matched Price multiplied by Quantity.

Once the data was ready, I used Excel PivotTables to analyse sales from different business perspectives. I created summaries to understand category-wise sales, 
product performance, customer locations, payment preferences, order statuses, and monthly sales trends.

I then used PivotCharts to present these results visually and developed an interactive dashboard using KPI cards, slicers, and date timelines. Users can filter the dashboard by category, 
customer location, order status, and month to explore different parts of the business.

Through this analysis, I found that Electronics was the highest-performing category, Refrigerators generated the highest sales among products, and Miami recorded the highest sales among customer locations.
I also identified that pending and cancelled orders together represented a significant portion of total orders.

Overall, this project helped me gain practical experience in Excel-based data analysis, PivotTables, PivotCharts, interactive dashboard development, 
business reporting, and identifying useful insights from raw data.


